E AX3059 631-region-escape.ax:46:10-16 region-escape "region `r` answers a value of type `String`, which may point into the memory the region reclaims" #"this has type `String`" ^45:15-16:"this region reclaims the result's allocation when its body ends" !"a `String` is a descriptor over a second block, a struct is a block and a closure is a record; every one of them would point at reclaimed memory" ?"compute a scalar such as (strLen value) inside the region and return it; if you need a reference result, allocate it outside the region"
E AX3059 631-region-escape.ax:50:16-19 region-escape "`out` is bound outside region `s`, and the value stored into it has type `String`" #"this store leaves the region" ^48:15-16:"this region ends before the outer binding is used" !"a store is the one escape channel a scope check can see; a call that stores the value for you is refused too, where the facts walk sees it" ?"move the reference allocation and this store outside the region, or bind the destination inside it; an outer binding may receive a scalar computed inside the region"
